  "title": "The nest as one small door: it works on open ground and gets buried in the lab",
  "question": "In the lab stills (bottom pair), does the colony's home read as buried under the plant litter, which is why a small door gets lost there while the long strip does not?",
  "context_md": "Test switch only; nothing in the game changed.\n\n**Top pair, the colony test bed**, seed 4 (the typical seed). Today the nest is painted as a 45-cell strip; with the switch it is a 5-cell door and every ant's home is that door. Magenta = empty ant, cyan = carrying food, red block = the food. Over 24 seeds the door cuts starvation 277 -> 209 and deaths among ants that never find the food 200 -> 125.\n\n**Bottom pair, the lab box**, seed 3, frames 6k/12k/20k/30k around the nest. The painted nest (white) sits about 10 cells under the litter mat. With the door, food carried home drops 5,396 -> 1,279 on every one of 12 seeds.\n\nSo the door is not shipping. The nest session is to build a real mouth that stays open to the surface.",
